B.VH=new A.aV(B.X4,["Splendid. Now all we want is the weapon.",u.h,u.p,u.X,u.o,"A watch stops when it breaks, Churlock. It does not pull out its own crown first. That is how one sets the hands. I should want a second opinion on the time, from something nobody thought to tamper with.","A clock that fell in a struggle would have broken its glass. Somebody opened that door and touched the hand. I should want a second opinion on the time, from something nobody thought to tamper with.","Four rings, old chap. Now, who makes those candles, when was this one lit, and how long does a ring take to burn?","The operator's word, and I believe every minute of it. From ten to eleven. Not a minute before.",u.N,"Notice when it begins, Churlock, not only that it has no gaps.","She meant to have somebody arrested at nine. And that somebody was not to be warned. I wonder if she was.",u.R,u.R,u.H,u.H,"Two went down and one came up. When were those steps last swept? The butler will know to the minute.","On top of the polish. So the question is when that handle was last polished. The butler will know to the minute.","Consider when it must have been written, Churlock, from what it says. Then consider when she died.","Hers alone. It proves little, as she'll be quick to tell you. It is the clock we must break, not the pin."],t.l)
B.NC=s(["Everyone has an alibi for five past eleven, Churlock. Suspiciously good ones. What if five past eleven is the wrong question?","Look again at the thing that told us the time, and at how it was found. Then look for something else in that cellar that keeps time, and ask Graham how it works.","Once you have the true minute, go round all five again. Three of them were already where they say by half past ten, and a fourth was latched out at ten. Who had not yet begun their alibi?","The Colonel heard something in the hall just after the game began. And the note she gave you could only have been written by somebody who was alive to hear a telephone call."],t.s)
B.acM=new A.m("what","What happened to her?","Victim is Mrs. \xc9claire Senclair, founder of Senclair Confections. One neat hole, Detective, straight through the shell, and every drop of custard let out of her. She went down like a punctured tyre. We traced where she fell in powdered sugar.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.abv=new A.m("weapon","What was the weapon?","Something long, thin and sharp. A skewer, a knitting needle, a meat thermometer. It isn't down here. It'd hide almost anywhere.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.P9=s([B.acM,B.abv,B.dE,B.cD],t.q)
B.ly=s(["candle"],t.s)
B.abU=new A.m("earlier","Could she have died earlier than eleven?","Custard doesn't tell the time to ten minutes, Detective. Half past ten, half past eleven, it sets the same. I said \u201caround eleven\u201d because that's what the hands said. If the hands are wrong, so am I.",B.ly,B.c,null)
B.TM=s([B.h6,B.h1,B.h3,B.h0,B.abU],t.q)
B.acW=new A.m("about","Tell me about Mrs. Senclair.","Strict, but fair. She'd had a face like thunder since the post came on Tuesday, mind. Something from the bank. She wouldn't say what.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.adT=new A.m("suspect","Who do you suspect?","I don't like to stir the pot... but the Colonel owes her a fortune, and Graham's not been himself for a month.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.ad9=new A.m("last","When did you last see her alive?","Twenty-five past ten. She put her head round my door to say goodnight and took a peppermint, same as always. I put the souffl\xe9 in five minutes after and never left it.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.PY=s([B.cQ,B.acW,B.adT,B.ad9,B.dD,B.cJ,B.dK,B.cP,B.cO,B.cS,B.cR],t.q)
B.aaR=new A.m("candle","Tell me about the ringed candles.","Hour candles, sir. I pour them myself and test each batch against the hall clock: one ring burns in ten minutes, neither more nor less. I light Madam's at ten precisely, when I latch the doors, and put it into her hand.",B.ly,B.c,null)
B.S0=s(["heelmarks","cocoadoor"],t.s)
B.adm=new A.m("polish","When were the cellar door and steps last cleaned?","At ten o'clock last night, sir, as on every night. When I have latched the doors I sweep the cellar steps and polish the door furniture. Whatever is on them now was put there after ten.",B.S0,B.c,null)
B.ab8=new A.m("began","When exactly did the chess begin?","At half past ten, sir. I entered the first move at 10:32. The Colonel was in his chair before I was.",B.cw,B.c,null)
B.Tq=s([B.mZ,B.dF,B.h2,B.aaR,B.adm,B.ab8,B.cH,B.cK,B.cI,B.cU,B.cV,B.cT],t.q)
B.abT=new A.m("suspect","Who do you suspect?","That gardener, sir. Forever lurking about below stairs. Not the niece: she was on the telephone, and the operator says so.",B.c,B.c,null)
B.q7=s(["graham/candle"],t.s)
B.ad_=new A.m("hall","Did you hear anything in the hall after the game began?","Now you mention it, sir, yes. We had barely opened. Twenty-five to eleven, say. \xc9claire's voice in the hall: \u201cThis had better be worth my slippers.\u201d And somebody answered her with a \u201cdarling\u201d. Then the cellar door.",B.c,B.q7,null)
B.PH=s([B.h5,B.h4,B.abT,B.ad_,B.eD,B.eC,B.cF,B.dH],t.q)
B.aej=new A.m("footsteps","Did anyone pass you on the landing?","Not a soul, darling. I was draped over that telephone table for forty minutes and nothing came up those stairs at all.",B.ef,B.c,null)
B.Kq=new A.O("auntnote","Aunt \xc9claire's Note","",0,"A note Tira says her aunt left on the telephone table: \u201cTira. I can hear you chattering on that telephone again. I am going down to lock the rack myself. Do not wait up. \xc9.S.\u201d",B.bk,B.I,null,B.j,B.c,!1,"tira")
B.aaU=new A.m("last","When did you last see your aunt?","At dinner, darling. But she left me this. I found it on the telephone table when I rang off at half past. You see? She went down there by herself, at eleven.",B.c,B.c,B.Kq)
B.acX=new A.m("before","Where were you at twenty to eleven?","Twenty to? Dressing, darling. One does not ring Madame Leine in curlers. Alone, naturally. Why twenty to? The watch said five past.",B.ly,B.q7,null)
B.TG=s(["watch","clock"],t.s)
B.ac8=new A.m("crown","There is cocoa on the hands that told us the time.","I went down for the port at nine, darling. I dust everything I touch. I dare say I brushed against it.",B.TG,B.c,null)
B.R3=s(["cocoadoor"],t.s)
B.OT=s(["graham/polish"],t.s)
B.abC=new A.m("door","Your cocoa is on the cellar door, on top of the polish.","Then Graham polished early, darling. He polishes everything. One can hardly be blamed for his timetable.",B.R3,B.OT,null)
B.TA=s(["cannoli/hall"],t.s)
B.adz=new A.m("darling","The Colonel heard someone say \u201cdarling\u201d to her at 10:35.","Everybody says darling, darling. Penny says it to the cat. ...We haven't a cat. To the dog, then.",B.c,B.TA,null)
B.R_=s(["cheques","bankletter"],t.s)
B.adE=new A.m("cheques","You have been signing her name on cheques.","A misunderstanding, darling. Auntie always said I might put things on her account. I merely put them on it rather more directly.",B.R_,B.c,null)
B.SM=s(["pinchest","pincrate"],t.s)
B.acQ=new A.m("pin","One of your hatpins is covered in custard.","I own forty hatpins, darling, and I lose one a week. Anyone might have picked it up off the hall table.",B.SM,B.c,null)
B.acx=new A.m("prints","Only your fingerprints are on the hatpin.","Well of course they are, it's mine. Whoever used it had the wit to wear gloves. I should have thought that cleared me.",B.aY,B.c,null)
